var e={id:`france`,name:`France`,localName:`France`,flag:`🇫🇷`,currency:`EUR`,language:`French`,greeting:{text:`Bonjour`,meaning:`Hello / Good day`},bestMonths:[4,5,6,9,10],tips:[`Always say "Bonjour" when entering a shop or café and "Merci, au revoir" when leaving; it changes how you are treated.`,`Service is included in restaurant bills; rounding up or leaving a euro or two for good service is plenty.`,`Many museums close one day a week: the Louvre and Orangerie on Tuesdays, Orsay and Versailles on Mondays. Check before planning.`,`Book timed-entry tickets online for the Louvre, Eiffel Tower, Versailles, Sainte-Chapelle and the Catacombs to skip long queues.`,`Restaurants typically serve lunch 12:00–14:00 and dinner from 19:30; outside those hours look for a brasserie with "service continu".`,`Watch for pickpockets on the Paris Metro, at Sacré-Cœur and around major sights, and on the Nice–Monaco trains.`],cities:[{id:`paris`,name:`Paris`,lat:48.8566,lng:2.3522,timezone:`Europe/Paris`,tagline:`Grand boulevards, world-class art and café life`,description:`The French capital pairs monumental landmarks and some of the world's greatest museums with intimate neighbourhoods, riverside walks and a food culture built around bakeries, bistros and markets.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`eiffel-tower`,name:`Eiffel Tower`,localName:`Tour Eiffel`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`sunset`],area:`Eiffel Tower`,lat:48.8584,lng:2.2945,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:5,description:`Gustave Eiffel's 1889 iron lattice tower, with sweeping city views from its second floor and summit. After dark it sparkles for five minutes at the top of every hour.`,tip:`Book a timed summit ticket online well ahead; taking the stairs to the second floor is cheaper and queues are shorter.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Eiffel Tower`},{id:`seine-river-cruise`,name:`Seine River Cruise (Bateaux Parisiens)`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`boat`,`night-view`,`sunset`,`kids`],area:`Eiffel Tower`,lat:48.8601,lng:2.2937,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:23,rating:4,description:`A one-hour glide past Notre-Dame, the Louvre and the Musée d'Orsay, departing from the foot of the Eiffel Tower. Most magical at dusk as the bridges light up.`,tip:`Time the cruise so you return just before the hour to see the tower sparkle from the water.`,indoor:!1},{id:`louvre`,name:`Louvre Museum`,localName:`Musée du Louvre`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Louvre & Tuileries`,lat:48.861,lng:2.3357,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:37,rating:5,description:`The world's most visited museum, a former royal palace housing the Mona Lisa, the Venus de Milo and the Winged Victory among some 35,000 works on display.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. A timed ticket is required; use the Carrousel or Porte des Lions entrances to avoid the pyramid queue.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Louvre`},{id:`musee-de-l-orangerie`,name:`Musée de l'Orangerie`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`impressionism`,`rainy-day`],area:`Louvre & Tuileries`,lat:48.8638,lng:2.3226,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`A serene gallery at the edge of the Tuileries built around Monet's immense Water Lilies panels, displayed in two oval rooms lit by daylight.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. Combine with a stroll through the Tuileries Garden toward the Louvre.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée de l'Orangerie`},{id:`musee-d-orsay`,name:`Musée d'Orsay`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`impressionism`,`rainy-day`],area:`Saint-Germain-des-Prés`,lat:48.86,lng:2.3266,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:5,description:`A grand Beaux-Arts railway station turned museum with the world's finest collection of Impressionist and Post-Impressionist art, from Monet and Renoir to Van Gogh.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Open late on Thursdays until 21:45, the quietest time to visit; peek through the giant clock window on the top floor.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée d'Orsay`},{id:`notre-dame`,name:`Notre-Dame Cathedral`,localName:`Cathédrale Notre-Dame de Paris`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`church`,`gothic`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Île de la Cité`,lat:48.853,lng:2.3499,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The Gothic masterpiece reopened in December 2024 after its painstaking post-fire restoration, its luminous cream-stone interior brighter than it has been in centuries.`,tip:`Entry is free; reserve an optional time slot on the official app to skip the walk-up line. The towers require a separate paid ticket.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Notre-Dame de Paris`},{id:`sainte-chapelle`,name:`Sainte-Chapelle`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`gothic`,`stained-glass`,`rainy-day`],area:`Île de la Cité`,lat:48.8554,lng:2.345,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:4,description:`A 13th-century royal chapel whose upper level is almost entirely walls of glowing stained glass, depicting more than 1,100 biblical scenes.`,tip:`Visit on a sunny day for the full effect, and book a timed slot to pass the security line faster.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sainte-Chapelle`},{id:`montmartre-sacre-coeur`,name:`Montmartre & Sacré-Cœur`,localName:`Basilique du Sacré-Cœur`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`free`,`village`],area:`Montmartre`,lat:48.8867,lng:2.3431,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The white-domed basilica crowns Paris's highest hill, surrounded by cobbled lanes, vineyards and the painters of Place du Tertre.`,tip:`Wander the quieter backstreets like Rue de l'Abreuvoir; ignore anyone offering string bracelets on the basilica steps.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sacré-Cœur, Paris`},{id:`moulin-rouge`,name:`Moulin Rouge`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`cabaret`,`show`,`iconic`],area:`Montmartre`,lat:48.8841,lng:2.3322,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:140,rating:4,description:`The legendary red-windmill cabaret, birthplace of the French cancan, still staging its feathered, sequinned revue twice nightly.`,tip:`Book weeks ahead; the show-only ticket is far better value than the dinner packages. Smart dress is expected.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Moulin Rouge`},{id:`le-marais-place-des-vosges`,name:`Le Marais & Place des Vosges`,category:`culture`,tags:[`walking`,`architecture`,`free`,`boutiques`],area:`Le Marais`,lat:48.8556,lng:2.3655,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Paris's oldest planned square anchors a district of aristocratic mansions, indie boutiques, falafel joints on Rue des Rosiers and lively Sunday streets.`,tip:`Unlike much of Paris, many Marais shops open on Sundays, making it a great Sunday afternoon stroll.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Le Marais`},{id:`marche-des-enfants-rouges`,name:`Marché des Enfants Rouges`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`lunch`,`street-food`],area:`Le Marais`,lat:48.8628,lng:2.3619,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`Paris's oldest covered market, dating from 1628, packed with stalls serving Moroccan couscous, Japanese bento, crêpes and Italian deli fare at shared tables.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Arrive before 12:30 to snag a seat at lunch.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Marché des Enfants Rouges`},{id:`arc-de-triomphe`,name:`Arc de Triomphe & Champs-Élysées`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`night-view`],area:`Champs-Élysées`,lat:48.8738,lng:2.295,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:4,description:`Napoleon's triumphal arch tops the city's grandest avenue; climb 284 steps for a star-shaped view of twelve boulevards radiating out to the Eiffel Tower.`,tip:`Reach it via the underground passage, never across the roundabout. The rooftop stays open late, making it great after dark.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Arc de Triomphe`},{id:`jardin-du-luxembourg`,name:`Luxembourg Gardens`,localName:`Jardin du Luxembourg`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`kids`,`picnic`],area:`Latin Quarter`,lat:48.8462,lng:2.3372,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Elegant formal gardens around the Luxembourg Palace, where Parisians lounge in green metal chairs and children sail rental toy boats on the Grand Bassin.`,tip:`Kids love the vintage puppet theatre and pony rides; grab a chair by the Medici Fountain for shade.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Jardin du Luxembourg`},{id:`shakespeare-and-company`,name:`Shakespeare and Company`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`books`,`literary`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Latin Quarter`,lat:48.8526,lng:2.3471,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A rambling, creaky English-language bookshop facing Notre-Dame, steeped in Lost Generation and Beat literary lore.`,tip:`Photos are not allowed inside; the adjoining café is good for a coffee with a cathedral view.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Shakespeare and Company (bookstore)`},{id:`grande-galerie-de-l-evolution`,name:`Grand Gallery of Evolution`,localName:`Grande Galerie de l'Évolution`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`natural-history`,`rainy-day`],area:`Latin Quarter`,lat:48.8423,lng:2.3561,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:4,description:`A soaring 19th-century glass-roofed hall in the Jardin des Plantes, where a parade of life-size taxidermy animals marches across the central floor.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. The botanical garden outside is free and the small zoo next door is a hit with children.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grande Galerie de l'Évolution`},{id:`palais-garnier`,name:`Palais Garnier`,localName:`Opéra Garnier`,category:`culture`,tags:[`architecture`,`opera`,`rainy-day`],area:`Opéra`,lat:48.872,lng:2.3316,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:4,description:`A lavish gilded opera house of marble staircases, a Chagall-painted ceiling and the gallery that inspired The Phantom of the Opera.`,tip:`Self-guided visits can be cut short on matinee and rehearsal days; check the schedule before going.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palais Garnier`},{id:`galeries-lafayette`,name:`Galeries Lafayette Haussmann`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`department-store`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`viewpoint`],area:`Opéra`,lat:48.8736,lng:2.332,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The flagship department store's Belle Époque stained-glass dome is a sight in itself, and its free rooftop terrace offers a fine view toward the Opéra and Eiffel Tower.`,tip:`Non-EU visitors spending over €100 in a day can claim a tax refund at the store's détaxe desk.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Galeries Lafayette Haussmann`},{id:`catacombs`,name:`Catacombs of Paris`,localName:`Catacombes de Paris`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`underground`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`Montparnasse`,lat:48.8338,lng:2.3324,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`A macabre 1.5 km walk through former quarry tunnels lined with the neatly stacked bones of some six million Parisians.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Timed tickets sell out days ahead; it is cool (about 14°C) underground with 243 steps in total.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Catacombs of Paris`},{id:`canal-saint-martin`,name:`Canal Saint-Martin`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`canal`,`bars`,`local`,`walking`],area:`Canal Saint-Martin`,lat:48.8716,lng:2.3644,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`Tree-lined locks and iron footbridges where young Parisians gather along the quays with wine at dusk, surrounded by natural-wine bars and bistros.`,tip:`Pick up supplies and join the locals picnicking on the canal edge on warm evenings.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Canal Saint-Martin`},{id:`versailles`,name:`Palace of Versailles`,localName:`Château de Versailles`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`day-trip`,`palace`,`gardens`],area:`Versailles`,lat:48.8049,lng:2.1204,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:5,description:`Louis XIV's colossal palace with the dazzling Hall of Mirrors, vast formal gardens and Marie Antoinette's estate, 40 minutes from central Paris by RER C.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Book a Passport ticket with a 9:00 palace slot, then do the gardens and Trianons; rent a bike or golf cart for the grounds.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Palace of Versailles`},{id:`musee-rodin`,name:`Rodin Museum`,localName:`Musée Rodin`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`sculpture`,`gardens`],area:`Invalides`,lat:48.8553,lng:2.3158,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`Rodin's former mansion and rose-filled sculpture garden, where The Thinker, The Kiss and The Gates of Hell sit among clipped hedges and lime trees.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. On a sunny day spend most of your time in the garden, which has the finest bronzes.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée Rodin`},{id:`les-invalides`,name:`Les Invalides & Napoleon's Tomb`,localName:`Hôtel des Invalides`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`history`,`military`,`rainy-day`],area:`Invalides`,lat:48.855,lng:2.3126,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`Louis XIV's golden-domed veterans' hospital, now home to the Army Museum and Napoleon's colossal red porphyry tomb beneath the dome.`,tip:`One ticket covers the Dome, tomb and Army Museum; it is open late on Tuesday evenings for part of the year.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Les Invalides`},{id:`pantheon`,name:`Panthéon`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`history`,`architecture`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`],area:`Latin Quarter`,lat:48.8462,lng:2.3464,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:4,description:`A neoclassical mausoleum crowning the Latin Quarter, where Voltaire, Victor Hugo, Marie Curie and Josephine Baker lie in the crypt beneath Foucault's swinging pendulum.`,tip:`The colonnade around the dome opens in the warmer months for an extra fee and gives a superb rooftop view.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Panthéon`},{id:`bourse-de-commerce`,name:`Bourse de Commerce – Pinault Collection`,localName:`Bourse de Commerce`,category:`museum`,tags:[`contemporary-art`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Les Halles`,lat:48.8628,lng:2.3428,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:4,description:`François Pinault's contemporary art collection inside a domed 18th-century grain exchange, reworked by Tadao Ando with a concrete cylinder beneath a painted glass cupola.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. Open until 21:00 on Fridays, and the free first Saturday evening of the month draws crowds.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Bourse de Commerce`},{id:`musee-picasso-paris`,name:`Picasso Museum Paris`,localName:`Musée Picasso`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Le Marais`,lat:48.8598,lng:2.3625,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`Thousands of works Picasso kept for himself, shown in the Hôtel Salé, one of the Marais's grandest 17th-century mansions.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Free on the first Sunday of the month, but book a slot online.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée Picasso`},{id:`rue-cler`,name:`Rue Cler Market Street`,localName:`Rue Cler`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`local`,`picnic`],area:`Eiffel Tower`,lat:48.8565,lng:2.3063,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A pedestrian market street of cheesemongers, bakeries, fishmongers and café terraces, ideal for assembling a picnic for the Champ de Mars.`,tip:`Most food shops close Sunday afternoon and all day Monday.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rue Cler`},{id:`trocadero`,name:`Trocadéro Gardens & Esplanade`,localName:`Jardins du Trocadéro`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`free`,`sunset`,`night-view`,`iconic`],area:`Eiffel Tower`,lat:48.8616,lng:2.2892,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The terrace of the Palais de Chaillot frames the classic head-on view of the Eiffel Tower across the Seine, best when the tower sparkles after dark.`,tip:`Come at sunrise for photos without the crowds, or on the hour after dark for the sparkle.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Trocadéro`},{id:`montparnasse-56`,name:`Montparnasse Tower Observation Deck`,localName:`Montparnasse 56`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`night-view`,`sunset`,`rainy-day`],area:`Montparnasse`,lat:48.8421,lng:2.3219,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:23,rating:4,description:`A 56th-floor observation deck and open-air rooftop on Paris's only skyscraper, with a 360-degree view that includes the Eiffel Tower itself.`,tip:`Usually far quieter than the Eiffel Tower; time your visit for sunset and stay as the lights come on.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Tour Montparnasse`},{id:`parc-des-buttes-chaumont`,name:`Buttes-Chaumont Park`,localName:`Parc des Buttes-Chaumont`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`picnic`,`viewpoint`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Buttes-Chaumont`,lat:48.8809,lng:2.3828,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A romantic hilly park built in an old quarry, with a cliff-top temple above a lake, grottoes, a waterfall and lawns full of local picnickers.`,tip:`Climb to the Temple de la Sibylle for the view toward Montmartre, then grab a drink at Rosa Bonheur by the park gates.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parc des Buttes Chaumont`},{id:`pere-lachaise`,name:`Père Lachaise Cemetery`,localName:`Cimetière du Père-Lachaise`,category:`culture`,tags:[`cemetery`,`free`,`history`,`walking`],area:`Père Lachaise`,lat:48.8614,lng:2.3933,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A hillside city of the dead with cobbled avenues and moss-covered tombs, the resting place of Chopin, Oscar Wilde, Édith Piaf and Jim Morrison.`,tip:`Pick up or download a map at the entrance; the cemetery is large and hilly, so wear comfortable shoes.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Père Lachaise Cemetery`},{id:`le-bon-marche`,name:`Le Bon Marché & La Grande Épicerie`,localName:`Le Bon Marché Rive Gauche`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`department-store`,`food`,`rainy-day`,`free`],area:`Saint-Germain-des-Prés`,lat:48.8509,lng:2.3245,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Paris's oldest department store, calmer and chicer than the Right Bank giants, with an escalator sculpture by architect Boileau and a spectacular food hall next door.`,tip:`La Grande Épicerie is perfect for edible souvenirs such as mustards, salted butter caramels and tins of sardines.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Le Bon Marché`},{id:`cafe-de-flore`,name:`Café de Flore`,category:`food`,tags:[`cafe`,`literary`,`people-watching`],area:`Saint-Germain-des-Prés`,lat:48.8541,lng:2.3325,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:3,description:`An Art Deco Left Bank café where Sartre and de Beauvoir once wrote, now a pricey but atmospheric spot for hot chocolate and people-watching.`,tip:`Sit on the terrace for the classic experience; Les Deux Magots is a few steps away for comparison.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Café de Flore`},{id:`galerie-vivienne`,name:`Galerie Vivienne & Palais-Royal`,localName:`Galerie Vivienne`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`covered-passage`,`architecture`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Palais-Royal`,lat:48.8665,lng:2.3399,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The most elegant of the 19th-century covered passages, with a mosaic floor and glass roof, beside the arcaded gardens and striped columns of the Palais-Royal.`,tip:`Walk on to Passage des Panoramas and Passage Jouffroy to the north for a rainy-day route under glass.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Galerie Vivienne`},{id:`jardin-d-acclimatation`,name:`Jardin d'Acclimatation`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`rides`,`park`,`animals`],area:`Bois de Boulogne`,lat:48.8784,lng:2.264,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A historic children's amusement garden in the Bois de Boulogne with vintage and modern rides, farm animals, play areas and a little train from Porte Maillot.`,tip:`Entry is cheap but rides need credit; a day pass is better value for kids who want several. The Fondation Louis Vuitton is next door.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Jardin d'Acclimatation`},{id:`caveau-de-la-huchette`,name:`Caveau de la Huchette`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`jazz`,`live-music`,`dancing`],area:`Latin Quarter`,lat:48.8527,lng:2.3465,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`A vaulted medieval cellar jazz club, open since 1946, where swing bands play and couples dance the lindy hop until the early hours.`,tip:`Music starts around 21:00; weekends are packed, so arrive early for a seat near the stage.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Caveau de la Huchette`},{id:`grand-mosque-of-paris`,name:`Grand Mosque of Paris`,localName:`Grande Mosquée de Paris`,category:`culture`,tags:[`architecture`,`tea`,`courtyard`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Latin Quarter`,lat:48.842,lng:2.3551,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A Hispano-Moorish mosque with a green-tiled minaret and tranquil courtyard garden, whose fig-shaded tearoom serves mint tea and pastries.`,tip:`The mosque is closed to visitors on Fridays and during prayer times; the tearoom is open daily.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grand Mosque of Paris`},{id:`giverny`,name:`Giverny (Monet's House & Gardens)`,localName:`Fondation Claude Monet`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`gardens`,`impressionism`],area:`Giverny`,lat:49.0756,lng:1.5335,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:65,rating:4,description:`Claude Monet's pink house and the flower garden and Japanese water-lily pond that he painted for decades, in a Normandy village an hour from Paris.`,tip:`Open only from April to early November. Take the train from Saint-Lazare to Vernon, then the shuttle bus; arrive at opening to beat the tour groups.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Giverny`}],foods:[{name:`Croissant`,localName:`Croissant au beurre`,description:`Flaky, all-butter crescent best eaten warm from a neighbourhood boulangerie at breakfast.`},{name:`French onion soup`,localName:`Soupe à l'oignon gratinée`,description:`Slow-caramelised onion broth under a crust of toasted bread and bubbling melted Comté.`},{name:`Steak frites`,localName:`Steak-frites`,description:`The bistro classic: seared entrecôte with crisp fries, often with béarnaise or peppercorn sauce.`},{name:`Croque monsieur`,localName:`Croque-monsieur`,description:`Toasted ham-and-cheese sandwich draped in béchamel and grilled golden; add a fried egg for a croque-madame.`},{name:`Macarons`,localName:`Macarons parisiens`,description:`Delicate almond-meringue sandwich cookies in endless flavours, made famous by Ladurée and Pierre Hermé.`},{name:`Crêpes`,localName:`Crêpes`,description:`Thin sweet pancakes from street stands, filled with Nutella, sugar and lemon, or flambéed Grand Marnier.`}]},{id:`nice`,name:`Nice`,lat:43.7102,lng:7.262,timezone:`Europe/Paris`,tagline:`Azure sea, pastel old town and Riviera light`,description:`The capital of the Côte d'Azur blends a sweeping seafront promenade with a Baroque Italianate old town, superb art museums and easy train hops to Monaco, Èze and the Riviera's prettiest villages.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`promenade-des-anglais`,name:`Promenade des Anglais`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`seafront`,`walking`,`sunset`,`free`],area:`Promenade des Anglais`,lat:43.6947,lng:7.2653,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Seven kilometres of palm-lined seafront curving around the Baie des Anges, perfect for strolling, cycling or sitting in the famous blue chairs.`,tip:`Rent a shared Vélo Bleu bike to ride the full length, and stop for a photo outside the pink-domed Hotel Negresco.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Promenade des Anglais`},{id:`musee-massena`,name:`Villa Masséna Museum`,localName:`Musée Masséna`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`belle-epoque`,`rainy-day`],area:`Promenade des Anglais`,lat:43.6955,lng:7.2609,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A Belle Époque seafront villa telling the story of Nice's glamorous Riviera heyday, with lovely gardens open free to the public.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays, like most of Nice's municipal museums.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée Masséna`},{id:`plage-beau-rivage`,name:`Beau Rivage Beach`,localName:`Plage Beau Rivage`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`beach-club`,`swimming`],area:`Promenade des Anglais`,lat:43.6953,lng:7.2716,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`One of Nice's stylish private beach clubs, with cushioned loungers, parasols and a restaurant right on the pebbles near the old town.`,tip:`Nice's beaches are pebbles, so bring water shoes; the public stretches either side are free.`,indoor:!1},{id:`vieux-nice`,name:`Old Town`,localName:`Vieux Nice`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`walking`,`free`,`architecture`],area:`Vieux Nice`,lat:43.6966,lng:7.276,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A tangle of narrow lanes and ochre façades hung with laundry, full of Baroque chapels, socca stands and buzzing terraces after dark.`,tip:`Duck into the Baroque Cathédrale Sainte-Réparate on Place Rossetti, then grab an ice cream next door.`,indoor:!1},{id:`cours-saleya-market`,name:`Cours Saleya Market`,localName:`Marché du Cours Saleya`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`flowers`,`local`],area:`Vieux Nice`,lat:43.6954,lng:7.2753,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`A vibrant open-air flower and produce market with Provençal fruit, olives, spices and hot socca, framed by pastel buildings.`,tip:`The food and flower market runs Tuesday to Sunday mornings; on Mondays the square hosts an antiques market instead.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Cours Saleya`},{id:`palais-lascaris`,name:`Palais Lascaris`,category:`museum`,tags:[`baroque`,`music`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vieux Nice`,lat:43.6977,lng:7.2774,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A 17th-century aristocratic palace with frescoed ceilings and a remarkable collection of historic musical instruments, hidden in the old town.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palais Lascaris`},{id:`fenocchio`,name:`Fenocchio Ice Cream`,localName:`Fenocchio`,category:`food`,tags:[`dessert`,`gelato`,`kids`],area:`Vieux Nice`,lat:43.6977,lng:7.2762,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:3,description:`A family-run glacier on Place Rossetti since 1966, famed for nearly a hundred flavours including lavender, olive and tomato-basil.`,indoor:!1},{id:`colline-du-chateau`,name:`Castle Hill`,localName:`Colline du Château`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`park`,`sunset`,`free`,`kids`],area:`Vieux Nice`,lat:43.695,lng:7.2808,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A wooded hilltop park with an artificial waterfall and the definitive panorama over the Baie des Anges, the old town's rooftops and the port.`,tip:`Climb the stairs from the end of Quai des États-Unis or take the free lift by the Tour Bellanda.`,indoor:!1},{id:`place-massena`,name:`Place Masséna`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`square`,`free`,`night-view`],area:`City Centre`,lat:43.6974,lng:7.27,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Nice's grand red-ochre square with a chequerboard pavement and Jaume Plensa's seven kneeling figures on poles, which glow in changing colours at night.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Place Masséna`},{id:`promenade-du-paillon`,name:`Promenade du Paillon`,category:`family`,tags:[`park`,`kids`,`free`,`fountains`],area:`City Centre`,lat:43.699,lng:7.273,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A long green park running from Place Masséna toward the theatre, with a shallow water mirror and mist jets that children love on hot days, plus big playgrounds.`,indoor:!1},{id:`musee-matisse`,name:`Matisse Museum`,localName:`Musée Matisse`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Cimiez`,lat:43.7196,lng:7.276,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A red Genoese villa among the olive groves of Cimiez holding works from every period of Matisse's career, who lived and died in Nice.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. Matisse is buried in the cemetery of the nearby Cimiez Monastery, whose gardens are free.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée Matisse (Nice)`},{id:`musee-chagall`,name:`Marc Chagall National Museum`,localName:`Musée National Marc Chagall`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Cimiez`,lat:43.709,lng:7.2693,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`A light-filled museum designed around Chagall's vivid Biblical Message cycle, with his stained-glass windows in the concert hall.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. Free on the first Sunday of the month.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée national Marc Chagall`},{id:`russian-orthodox-cathedral`,name:`St Nicholas Russian Orthodox Cathedral`,localName:`Cathédrale Saint-Nicolas`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Saint-Philippe`,lat:43.7039,lng:7.2531,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`The largest Russian Orthodox cathedral in Western Europe, with green-and-gold onion domes and a richly decorated icon-filled interior.`,tip:`Shoulders and knees must be covered; it closes during services.`,indoor:!0},{id:`port-lympia`,name:`Port Lympia`,localName:`Port de Nice`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`harbour`,`bars`,`restaurants`,`sunset`],area:`Le Port`,lat:43.6967,lng:7.2858,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`Nice's colourful harbour, lined with Italianate façades, fishing boats and yachts, and a relaxed string of wine bars and seafood restaurants.`,tip:`Walk around the eastern quay at sunset for views back over the bobbing pointus boats.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Port Lympia`},{id:`chez-pipo`,name:`Chez Pipo`,category:`food`,tags:[`socca`,`local`,`cheap-eats`],area:`Le Port`,lat:43.7012,lng:7.2856,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`A beloved socca house since 1923, baking crisp chickpea pancakes in a wood-fired oven and serving them on shared tables with rosé.`,tip:`Opens in the late afternoon; expect a queue at dinner time. Order several portions of socca with pissaladière.`,indoor:!0},{id:`coastal-path-coco-beach`,name:`Coastal Path to Coco Beach`,category:`nature`,tags:[`walking`,`coastal`,`swimming`,`free`],area:`Mont Boron`,lat:43.693,lng:7.294,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A short seaside walk past the port to the rocky coves of Coco Beach, where locals swim off flat rocks in clear turquoise water.`,tip:`Bring swimwear and water shoes; there are no facilities, so carry drinks.`,indoor:!1},{id:`parc-phoenix`,name:`Parc Phoenix`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`botanical`,`animals`],area:`Arénas`,lat:43.6667,lng:7.215,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A botanical and zoological park near the airport with one of Europe's largest greenhouses, a lake, lemurs and playgrounds.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parc Phoenix`},{id:`villa-ephrussi-de-rothschild`,name:`Villa Ephrussi de Rothschild`,category:`culture`,tags:[`gardens`,`villa`,`half-day`],area:`Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat`,lat:43.6957,lng:7.3322,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:22,rating:4,description:`A rose-pink Belle Époque villa on the Cap Ferrat isthmus with nine themed gardens and dancing musical fountains overlooking two bays.`,tip:`Reach it by bus 15 from Nice; the house interior makes it a reasonable option on a showery day.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Villa Ephrussi de Rothschild`},{id:`eze-village`,name:`Èze Village`,localName:`Èze`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`village`,`viewpoint`,`hiking`],area:`Èze`,lat:43.7277,lng:7.3617,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:4,description:`A medieval eagle's-nest village perched 400 m above the sea, crowned by a cactus-filled exotic garden with jaw-dropping coastal views.`,tip:`Take bus 82 or 602 up from Nice, then hike down the steep Nietzsche Path to Èze-sur-Mer station and catch the train back.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Èze`},{id:`monaco-monte-carlo`,name:`Monaco & Monte-Carlo`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`casino`,`harbour`,`glamour`],area:`Monaco`,lat:43.7384,lng:7.4246,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:4,description:`The tiny principality of superyachts and Grand Prix streets, with the cliff-top old town of Monaco-Ville, the Prince's Palace and the Belle Époque Monte-Carlo Casino.`,tip:`The train from Nice takes about 20 minutes. Catch the changing of the guard at the palace at 11:55.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Monaco`},{id:`cathedrale-sainte-reparate`,name:`Sainte-Réparate Cathedral`,localName:`Cathédrale Sainte-Réparate`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`baroque`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vieux Nice`,lat:43.6972,lng:7.2758,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Nice's 17th-century Baroque cathedral on Place Rossetti, with a glazed-tile dome and a richly gilded, stucco-laden interior.`,tip:`Respect services and cover your shoulders; afterwards the square is the spot for an ice cream.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Nice Cathedral`},{id:`monastere-de-cimiez`,name:`Cimiez Monastery & Gardens`,localName:`Monastère de Cimiez`,category:`nature`,tags:[`gardens`,`free`,`viewpoint`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Cimiez`,lat:43.7202,lng:7.2788,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A Franciscan monastery whose free rose-filled garden overlooks the city and sea, with the cemetery where Matisse and Raoul Dufy are buried.`,tip:`Pair it with the Matisse Museum and Roman ruins a few minutes away in the same olive park.`,indoor:!1},{id:`musee-archeologie-cimiez`,name:`Archaeology Museum & Roman Ruins of Cimiez`,localName:`Musée d'Archéologie de Nice-Cimiez`,category:`museum`,tags:[`roman`,`history`,`ruins`],area:`Cimiez`,lat:43.7192,lng:7.2753,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`The remains of Roman Cemenelum, with baths, streets and a small amphitheatre, plus a museum of finds from the ancient town.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays, like the other municipal museums.`,indoor:!1},{id:`musee-des-beaux-arts-nice`,name:`Nice Fine Arts Museum`,localName:`Musée des Beaux-Arts Jules Chéret`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`,`villa`],area:`Les Baumettes`,lat:43.6946,lng:7.249,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A Belle Époque villa built for a Ukrainian princess, displaying paintings from the 17th to 20th centuries including works by Jules Chéret, Dufy and Van Dongen.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. Uphill from the western end of the Promenade.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée des Beaux-Arts de Nice`},{id:`marche-de-la-liberation`,name:`Libération Market`,localName:`Marché de la Libération`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`local`,`cheap-eats`],area:`Libération`,lat:43.7135,lng:7.2618,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`The market where Niçois actually shop: a lively morning spread of farm produce, cheese, fish and socca on Place du Général de Gaulle, a short tram ride north.`,tip:`Runs Tuesday to Sunday mornings; prices and atmosphere are more local than at Cours Saleya.`,indoor:!1},{id:`avenue-jean-medecin`,name:`Avenue Jean-Médecin`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping-street`,`free`,`department-store`],area:`City Centre`,lat:43.701,lng:7.268,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Nice's main shopping boulevard, run through by the tram, lined with high-street chains, the Galeries Lafayette and the Nice Étoile mall.`,tip:`Nice Étoile mall halfway up the avenue is a handy indoor retreat on a rainy afternoon.`,indoor:!1},{id:`rue-bonaparte`,name:`Rue Bonaparte & Petit Marais Bars`,localName:`Rue Bonaparte`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`local`,`restaurants`],area:`Le Port`,lat:43.7,lng:7.283,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:3,description:`A buzzy little district between the old town and the port, packed with wine bars, cocktail spots and bistros that spill onto pavements on warm nights.`,tip:`Busiest from Thursday to Saturday; Place du Pin nearby is also good for drinks by the harbour.`,indoor:!1},{id:`opera-de-nice`,name:`Nice Opera House`,localName:`Opéra de Nice`,category:`culture`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`show`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vieux Nice`,lat:43.6955,lng:7.2727,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:3,description:`A red-and-gold Italianate opera house just behind the seafront, staging opera, ballet and symphony concerts from autumn to spring.`,tip:`Last-minute and upper-tier seats are often very affordable.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Opéra de Nice`},{id:`fort-du-mont-alban`,name:`Mont Boron & Fort du Mont Alban`,localName:`Fort du Mont Alban`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hiking`,`viewpoint`,`free`,`forest`],area:`Mont Boron`,lat:43.7046,lng:7.2995,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Pine-forest trails across Mont Boron lead to a 16th-century hilltop fort with views over both the Baie des Anges and Villefranche's harbour.`,tip:`Take bus 14 most of the way up if you do not fancy the climb; bring water.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fort du Mont Alban`},{id:`villefranche-sur-mer`,name:`Villefranche-sur-Mer`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`village`,`beach`,`swimming`,`half-day`],area:`Villefranche-sur-Mer`,lat:43.7041,lng:7.3114,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`A pastel fishing village wrapped around one of the Riviera's deepest natural harbours, with a sandy beach, a vaulted medieval street and Cocteau's painted chapel.`,tip:`Only seven minutes by train from Nice. The Rue Obscure, a covered 13th-century street, is easy to miss.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Villefranche-sur-Mer`},{id:`cap-ferrat-coastal-path`,name:`Cap Ferrat Coastal Path`,localName:`Sentier du littoral de Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hiking`,`coastal`,`free`,`swimming`],area:`Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat`,lat:43.685,lng:7.336,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A rocky shoreline trail looping around the tip of Cap Ferrat past millionaires' villas, a lighthouse and swimming coves of startling turquoise water.`,tip:`Start from Saint-Jean port; the path can close in rough seas. Paloma Beach makes a good swim stop.`,indoor:!1},{id:`saint-paul-de-vence`,name:`Saint-Paul-de-Vence`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`village`,`art`,`medieval`],area:`Saint-Paul-de-Vence`,lat:43.6966,lng:7.1222,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A ramparted hill village of galleries and cobbled lanes long loved by artists, with the Fondation Maeght's modern art collection in the pines just outside.`,tip:`Bus 400 runs from Nice. Have a drink on the terrace of La Colombe d'Or, whose walls hang with Picassos and Mirós.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Saint-Paul-de-Vence`},{id:`antibes`,name:`Antibes & Picasso Museum`,localName:`Antibes`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`old-town`,`art`,`beach`],area:`Antibes`,lat:43.5808,lng:7.1283,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`A ramparted old town above a superyacht harbour, with a covered Provençal market and the seafront Château Grimaldi where Picasso painted in 1946.`,tip:`Trains from Nice take about 20 minutes. The Picasso Museum is closed on Mondays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Antibes`},{id:`grasse`,name:`Grasse Perfume Town`,localName:`Grasse`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`perfume`,`shopping`,`rainy-day`],area:`Grasse`,lat:43.6584,lng:6.9225,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`The world capital of perfume, where free guided tours of the Fragonard and Molinard factories show how scent is made, and you can blend your own.`,tip:`The International Perfume Museum and Fragonard factory tours make it a good choice for a grey day. Trains run from Nice in about 70 minutes.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grasse`},{id:`cannes`,name:`Cannes & La Croisette`,localName:`Cannes`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`glamour`,`beach`,`shopping`],area:`Cannes`,lat:43.551,lng:7.0174,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`The film festival city's palm-lined Croisette promenade, the Palais des Festivals red-carpet steps and the old Le Suquet quarter overlooking the bay.`,tip:`Take the train (about 35 minutes), then a boat to the peaceful Lérins Islands for the afternoon.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Cannes`}],foods:[{name:`Socca`,localName:`Socca`,description:`A thin, crisp chickpea-flour pancake baked in a wood-fired oven, eaten hot with black pepper.`},{name:`Salade niçoise`,localName:`Salade niçoise`,description:`Tomatoes, hard-boiled egg, tuna or anchovies, black Niçoise olives and raw vegetables; locals insist no potatoes or green beans.`},{name:`Pan bagnat`,localName:`Pan bagnat`,description:`A round bread roll soaked in olive oil and stuffed with the ingredients of a salade niçoise, the classic beach lunch.`},{name:`Pissaladière`,localName:`Pissaladière`,description:`Focaccia-like tart topped with slow-cooked sweet onions, anchovies and black olives.`},{name:`Stuffed vegetables`,localName:`Petits farcis niçois`,description:`Courgettes, tomatoes, peppers and onions stuffed with seasoned meat, herbs and breadcrumbs, then baked.`},{name:`Swiss chard pie`,localName:`Tourte de blettes`,description:`A surprising sweet pie of Swiss chard, raisins, pine nuts and apple, dusted with sugar.`}]},{id:`lyon`,name:`Lyon`,lat:45.764,lng:4.8357,timezone:`Europe/Paris`,tagline:`Two rivers, Roman hills and the best bouchons in France`,description:`France's gastronomic capital sits where the Rhône meets the Saône, with a Renaissance old town laced with hidden traboules, a basilica-crowned Roman hill, silk-weavers' Croix-Rousse and a bouchon on every corner.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`basilica-of-notre-dame-de-fourviere`,name:`Basilica of Notre-Dame de Fourvière`,localName:`Basilique Notre-Dame de Fourvière`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`church`,`viewpoint`,`architecture`,`free`],area:`Fourvière`,lat:45.7625,lng:4.8225,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The white, four-towered basilica watching over the city from Fourvière hill, with a dazzling mosaic interior and the best panorama of Lyon from its esplanade.`,tip:`Ride the funicular up from Vieux Lyon and walk back down through the Jardin du Rosaire.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Basilica of Notre-Dame de Fourvière`},{id:`vieux-lyon`,name:`Old Lyon`,localName:`Vieux Lyon`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`old-town`,`renaissance`,`walking`,`unesco`,`free`],area:`Vieux Lyon`,lat:45.76222,lng:4.82667,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`One of Europe's largest Renaissance quarters, with pastel merchants' houses, spiral-staircase courtyards and cobbled lanes lined with bouchons along Rue Saint-Jean.`,tip:`Push open the doors at 27 Rue Saint-Jean and 54 Rue Saint-Jean to walk through traboules, the covered passages between streets.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Vieux Lyon`},{id:`lyon-cathedral`,name:`Lyon Cathedral`,localName:`Cathédrale Saint-Jean-Baptiste`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`gothic`,`architecture`,`free`],area:`Vieux Lyon`,lat:45.76056,lng:4.8275,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A Romanesque-Gothic cathedral on the banks of the Saône, famous for its 14th-century astronomical clock and jewel-toned medieval stained glass.`,tip:`The astronomical clock sets its figures in motion at noon, 2pm, 3pm and 4pm.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Lyon Cathedral`},{id:`ancient-theatre-of-fourviere`,name:`Ancient Theatre of Fourvière`,localName:`Théâtre antique de Fourvière`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`roman`,`ruins`,`history`,`viewpoint`,`free`],area:`Fourvière`,lat:45.75972,lng:4.81972,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A Roman theatre built around 15 BC for the city of Lugdunum, its tiered stone seats still used for concerts during the summer Nuits de Fourvière festival.`,tip:`Entry to the ruins is free; check the Nuits de Fourvière programme for June and July shows under the stars.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ancient Theatre of Fourvière`},{id:`lugdunum-museum`,name:`Lugdunum Museum`,localName:`Lugdunum – Musée et théâtres romains`,category:`museum`,tags:[`roman`,`history`,`archaeology`,`rainy-day`],area:`Fourvière`,lat:45.76042,lng:4.81991,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:4,description:`A striking concrete museum buried in the hillside beside the Roman theatres, displaying mosaics, inscriptions and the bronze Claudian Table from Roman Lyon.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; the windows frame a great view straight down onto the theatre.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Lugdunum (museum)`},{id:`parc-des-hauteurs`,name:`Parc des Hauteurs`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`walking`,`viewpoint`,`free`],area:`Fourvière`,lat:45.7627,lng:4.8237,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A string of green spaces and footpaths across the top of Fourvière, linked by the old Loyasse footbridge, with quiet benches and city views away from the crowds.`,tip:`Combine it with the Jardin des Curiosités in Saint-Just for a little-known sunset viewpoint.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parc des Hauteurs`},{id:`musee-miniature-et-cinema`,name:`Miniature and Cinema Museum`,localName:`Musée Miniature et Cinéma`,category:`family`,tags:[`film`,`miniatures`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vieux Lyon`,lat:45.76188,lng:4.8273,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`A Renaissance house packed with astonishingly detailed miniature rooms plus original props, costumes and special-effects models from well-known films.`,tip:`Tuesdays it opens only in the afternoon; allow extra time if you love film trivia.`,indoor:!0},{id:`musee-gadagne`,name:`Gadagne Museums`,localName:`Musées Gadagne`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`puppets`,`guignol`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vieux Lyon`,lat:45.76417,lng:4.8275,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:3,description:`Two museums in Vieux Lyon's largest Renaissance mansion: one tells the story of the city, the other celebrates world puppetry and Lyon's own Guignol.`,tip:`The hidden hanging garden café on the upper floor is a calm spot for a coffee.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée Gadagne`},{id:`fresque-des-lyonnais`,name:`Fresco of the Lyonnais`,localName:`Fresque des Lyonnais`,category:`culture`,tags:[`street-art`,`mural`,`photo-spot`,`free`],area:`Quai Saint-Vincent`,lat:45.76811,lng:4.82803,durationHours:.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A trompe-l'oeil mural covering a whole building by the Saône, where famous Lyonnais from the Lumière brothers to Paul Bocuse peer out of painted windows.`,tip:`See if you can spot Saint-Exupéry and the Little Prince sitting together on the top floor.`,indoor:!1},{id:`place-des-terreaux`,name:`Place des Terreaux`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`square`,`fountain`,`architecture`,`free`],area:`Presqu'île (Terreaux)`,lat:45.76748,lng:4.83349,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A grand square framed by the 17th-century City Hall and the fine-arts museum, centred on Bartholdi's horse-drawn fountain and lined with café terraces.`,tip:`Come after dark, when the façades and fountain are lit up and the terraces fill.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Place des Terreaux`},{id:`museum-of-fine-arts-of-lyon`,name:`Museum of Fine Arts of Lyon`,localName:`Musée des Beaux-Arts de Lyon`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`paintings`,`antiquities`,`rainy-day`],area:`Presqu'île (Terreaux)`,lat:45.7669,lng:4.8336,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:4,description:`One of France's largest art museums, set in a former Benedictine abbey, ranging from Egyptian antiquities to Rubens, Monet and Picasso.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays; the abbey's cloister garden is free to enter and a peaceful break from the Presqu'île.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of Fine Arts of Lyon`},{id:`opera-de-lyon`,name:`Lyon Opera House`,localName:`Opéra Nouvel`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`architecture`,`performance`],area:`Presqu'île (Terreaux)`,lat:45.76783,lng:4.83661,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:3,description:`A 19th-century opera house crowned by Jean Nouvel's glass barrel vault, staging opera, ballet and concerts in a striking modern auditorium.`,tip:`Book ahead for opera nights; reduced-price tickets for young people are often available.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Opéra de Lyon`},{id:`rue-merciere`,name:`Rue Mercière`,category:`food`,tags:[`restaurants`,`pedestrian`,`dinner`,`historic`],area:`Presqu'île (Cordeliers)`,lat:45.7625,lng:4.83278,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`A narrow pedestrian street of 16th-century printers' houses now lined end to end with restaurant terraces, lively on warm evenings.`,tip:`Look for the official 'Les Bouchons Lyonnais' plaque to tell genuine bouchons from tourist menus.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rue Mercière`},{id:`place-bellecour`,name:`Place Bellecour`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`square`,`statue`,`free`,`meeting-point`],area:`Presqu'île (Bellecour)`,lat:45.7575,lng:4.83222,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`One of the largest open squares in Europe, its red gravel centred on an equestrian statue of Louis XIV with Fourvière rising behind.`,tip:`The tourist office is on the square, and the Ferris wheel appears here in winter.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Place Bellecour`},{id:`grand-hotel-dieu`,name:`Grand Hôtel-Dieu`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`architecture`,`boutiques`,`courtyards`,`free`],area:`Presqu'île (Bellecour)`,lat:45.75833,lng:4.83639,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A grand former hospital on the Rhône, centuries old and crowned by a Soufflot dome, now restored into boutiques, cafés and a hotel around elegant courtyards.`,tip:`Wander the arcaded cloisters even if you are not shopping; the dome bar has a terrace view.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Hôtel-Dieu de Lyon`},{id:`la-croix-rousse`,name:`La Croix-Rousse`,category:`culture`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`silk`,`walking`,`viewpoint`,`free`],area:`Croix-Rousse`,lat:45.77944,lng:4.8275,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The 'hill that works', once home to thousands of silk weavers, now a village-like district of tall workshop buildings, steep stairways and a relaxed bohemian feel.`,tip:`Walk up the Montée de la Grande Côte for a sweeping view back over the city.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`La Croix-Rousse`},{id:`cour-des-voraces`,name:`Cour des Voraces`,category:`culture`,tags:[`traboule`,`history`,`architecture`,`free`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Croix-Rousse slopes`,lat:45.77194,lng:4.83472,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The most famous traboule, a courtyard with a monumental six-storey open stairway that linked weavers' homes and sheltered silk workers during their 19th-century revolts.`,tip:`These are residential buildings: keep voices down and close the doors behind you.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Cour des Voraces`},{id:`mur-des-canuts`,name:`Silk Workers' Wall`,localName:`Mur des Canuts`,category:`culture`,tags:[`street-art`,`mural`,`photo-spot`,`free`],area:`Croix-Rousse`,lat:45.77793,lng:4.82797,durationHours:.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A huge, regularly repainted trompe-l'oeil mural of everyday Croix-Rousse life, so convincing that the stairs look walkable.`,indoor:!1},{id:`halles-de-lyon-paul-bocuse`,name:`Les Halles de Lyon Paul Bocuse`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`gourmet`,`cheese`,`oysters`,`rainy-day`],area:`Part-Dieu`,lat:45.76283,lng:4.85055,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:5,description:`Lyon's covered gourmet market, with dozens of top cheesemongers, charcutiers, pâtissiers and oyster bars where locals linger over a glass of white.`,tip:`Go late morning on a weekend for oysters and white wine at the counters; closed Monday.`,indoor:!0},{id:`parc-de-la-tete-d-or`,name:`Parc de la Tête d'Or`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`lake`,`gardens`,`picnic`,`free`],area:`Brotteaux`,lat:45.78,lng:4.854,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`One of France's largest urban parks, with a boating lake, rose gardens and grand 19th-century glasshouses, all free to explore.`,tip:`Rent a rowing boat on the lake in summer, or head to the big greenhouses on a cold day.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parc de la Tête d'or`},{id:`lyon-zoo`,name:`Lyon Zoo`,localName:`Zoo de Lyon`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`kids`,`animals`,`free`],area:`Brotteaux`,lat:45.7775,lng:4.85639,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A free zoo inside the Parc de la Tête d'Or, whose African plain lets giraffes, zebras and lions roam in a naturalistic setting.`,tip:`Pair it with a picnic in the park; the animals are most active in the morning.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lyon Zoo`},{id:`musee-d-art-contemporain`,name:`Museum of Contemporary Art`,localName:`Musée d'art contemporain de Lyon`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`contemporary`,`rainy-day`],area:`Cité Internationale`,lat:45.78417,lng:4.8525,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A Renzo Piano-designed space at the edge of the Tête d'Or park that reinvents itself with each big temporary exhibition and hosts the Lyon Biennale.`,tip:`It closes between exhibitions, so check the dates before heading out; closed Monday and Tuesday.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée d'art contemporain de Lyon`},{id:`musee-des-confluences`,name:`Musée des Confluences`,category:`museum`,tags:[`science`,`anthropology`,`architecture`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Confluence`,lat:45.73291,lng:4.8183,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:5,description:`A deconstructivist steel-and-glass cloud at the tip of the peninsula, exploring the origins of life, species and societies with dinosaurs, meteorites and world cultures.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; book a timed ticket online on weekends and school holidays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée des Confluences`},{id:`confluence-shopping-centre`,name:`Confluence Shopping Centre`,localName:`Centre commercial Confluence`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`mall`,`riverside`,`modern-architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Confluence`,lat:45.74115,lng:4.81728,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A bright modern mall on the Saône docks, the centrepiece of the regenerated Confluence district with its colourful cube buildings and waterside promenade.`,tip:`Walk the quays past the Orange Cube and the Green Cube for the best of the new architecture.`,indoor:!0},{id:`le-sucre`,name:`Le Sucre`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`club`,`rooftop`,`electronic`,`dj`,`late-night`],area:`Confluence`,lat:45.73664,lng:4.81501,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:3,description:`A rooftop club on top of La Sucrière, a former sugar warehouse, with Saône views and one of France's most respected electronic music programmes.`,tip:`Sunday sessions start in the early evening; bring an original ID, as photocopies are refused.`,indoor:!1},{id:`chrd`,name:`Resistance and Deportation History Centre`,localName:`Centre d'histoire de la résistance et de la déportation`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`ww2`,`rainy-day`],area:`Jean Macé`,lat:45.74694,lng:4.83581,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:4,description:`A moving museum in the building where the Gestapo once held prisoners, telling the story of Lyon as 'capital of the Resistance' in the Second World War.`,tip:`Closed Mondays and Tuesdays; the audio guide adds valuable personal testimonies.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Centre d'histoire de la résistance et de la déportation`},{id:`institut-lumiere`,name:`Institut Lumière`,category:`museum`,tags:[`film`,`history`,`cinema`,`rainy-day`],area:`Monplaisir`,lat:45.74521,lng:4.87041,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`The Lumière family villa, beside the hangar where the brothers shot the world's first film in 1895, now a museum of early cinema with a repertory screen.`,tip:`Stay for an evening screening of a classic film in the cinema across the garden.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Institut Lumière`},{id:`berges-du-rhone`,name:`Rhône Riverbanks`,localName:`Berges du Rhône`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`riverside`,`bars`,`barges`,`sunset`,`cycling`],area:`Rive Gauche (Guillotière)`,lat:45.756,lng:4.8435,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Five kilometres of car-free promenade on the Rhône's left bank, busy with joggers by day and with drinkers on the moored barge bars (péniches) after dark.`,tip:`Grab a drink on a péniche near the Pont de la Guillotière as the sun sets behind Fourvière.`,indoor:!1},{id:`saone-river-cruise`,name:`Saône River Cruise`,localName:`Les Bateaux Lyonnais`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`boat`,`river`,`sightseeing`,`sunset`],area:`Quai des Célestins`,lat:45.76094,lng:4.83075,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:3,description:`An hour-long sightseeing cruise along the Saône and Rhône, gliding past Vieux Lyon, Fourvière and the Confluence with commentary.`,tip:`Take an early-evening sailing for golden light on the old town façades.`,indoor:!1},{id:`grand-parc-miribel-jonage`,name:`Grand Parc Miribel-Jonage`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`lake`,`swimming`,`cycling`,`kayak`,`outdoors`],area:`Vaulx-en-Velin`,lat:45.8058,lng:4.9364,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A vast nature park on the Rhône just outside the city, with lakes for swimming and paddling, bike trails, horse riding and summer water sports.`,tip:`In summer the Atol beach is lifeguarded; rent bikes or kayaks at the lake.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Grand parc de Miribel-Jonage`},{id:`perouges`,name:`Pérouges`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`medieval`,`village`,`walking`],area:`Ain (35 km)`,lat:45.90735,lng:5.17273,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A perfectly preserved medieval hilltop village of cobbled lanes and half-timbered houses, a favourite film set an easy half-day from Lyon.`,tip:`Try the galette de Pérouges, a thin sugared tart sold warm in the village square.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pérouges`},{id:`vienne-roman-town`,name:`Vienne Roman Town`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`roman`,`ruins`,`history`],area:`Vienne (30 km)`,lat:45.52548,lng:4.87425,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:3,description:`A Rhône town 20 minutes south by train, with a near-intact Roman temple of Augustus and Livia, a hillside Roman theatre and a Gallo-Roman museum across the river.`,tip:`Go in early July for the Jazz à Vienne festival in the ancient theatre.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Temple of Augustus and Livia`},{id:`oingt-beaujolais`,name:`Oingt and the Beaujolais`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`village`,`countryside`],area:`Beaujolais (35 km)`,lat:45.9486,lng:4.5831,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A golden-stone hilltop village at the heart of the 'Pierres Dorées' Beaujolais, surrounded by vineyards and wine cellars offering tastings.`,tip:`A car or a guided wine tour is the easiest way to link several villages and cellars.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Oingt`},{id:`annecy`,name:`Annecy`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`lake`,`alps`,`old-town`],area:`Haute-Savoie (100 km)`,lat:45.916,lng:6.133,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An Alpine lakeside town with canal-laced old streets and strikingly clear turquoise water, about two hours from Lyon by train.`,tip:`Rent a bike for the flat lakeside cycle path or take a boat tour of the lake.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Annecy`}],foods:[{name:`Pike quenelle`,localName:`Quenelle de brochet`,description:`A light, soufflé-like dumpling of pike and panade baked in a rich crayfish Nantua sauce until puffed and golden.`},{name:`Lyonnaise salad`,localName:`Salade lyonnaise`,description:`Frisée lettuce tossed with crisp bacon lardons, garlic croutons and a soft poached egg in a sharp mustard vinaigrette.`},{name:`Silk weaver's cheese`,localName:`Cervelle de canut`,description:`Fresh fromage blanc whipped with shallots, chives, herbs, vinegar and oil, eaten as a starter with bread or potatoes.`},{name:`Fireman's apron`,localName:`Tablier de sapeur`,description:`Beef tripe marinated in white wine and mustard, breaded and fried, served with a gribiche or garlic sauce.`},{name:`Andouillette`,localName:`Andouillette`,description:`A coarse, pungent sausage of pork chitterlings, usually grilled and served with mustard sauce and potatoes.`},{name:`Pink praline tart`,localName:`Tarte aux pralines`,description:`A shortcrust tart filled with crushed pink sugar-coated almonds melted with cream into a sticky, vivid pink filling.`}]},{id:`marseille`,name:`Marseille`,lat:43.2965,lng:5.3698,timezone:`Europe/Paris`,tagline:`Old port, white cliffs and the bouillabaisse of the Med`,description:`France's oldest city is a loud, sunlit Mediterranean port where fishermen still sell their catch on the Vieux-Port, the gilded Bonne Mère watches from her hill, the Panier's lanes climb above the MuCEM and the limestone Calanques plunge into turquoise coves.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`notre-dame-de-la-garde`,name:`Notre-Dame de la Garde`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`church`,`viewpoint`,`architecture`,`free`],area:`Notre-Dame de la Garde`,lat:43.28394,lng:5.37106,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The 'Bonne Mère', a neo-Byzantine basilica topped by a gilded Virgin on the city's highest point, with ship models and votive paintings inside and a 360-degree view over the port, islands and hills.`,tip:`Take bus 60 or the little tourist train up and walk back down through the Roucas-Blanc lanes; the wind on top can be fierce.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Notre-Dame de la Garde`},{id:`vieux-port`,name:`Old Port`,localName:`Vieux-Port`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`harbour`,`fish-market`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Vieux-Port`,lat:43.29513,lng:5.37446,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The 2,600-year-old harbour at the heart of the city, ringed by café terraces and bobbing sailboats, with fishermen selling the morning catch on the Quai des Belges under Norman Foster's mirrored canopy.`,tip:`Be on the Quai des Belges around 8–10am for the fish market, and come back at dusk when the quays glow and the terraces fill.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Old Port of Marseille`},{id:`mucem`,name:`MuCEM`,localName:`Musée des Civilisations de l'Europe et de la Méditerranée`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`architecture`,`history`,`mediterranean`,`rainy-day`],area:`Joliette (J4)`,lat:43.2968,lng:5.3611,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:5,description:`A cube of lace-like concrete on the harbour mouth, linked by a slender footbridge to Fort Saint-Jean, with exhibitions on the peoples and cultures of the Mediterranean and a rooftop terrace over the sea.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays; the rooftop, footbridges and fort gardens are free even without an exhibition ticket.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum of European and Mediterranean Civilisations`},{id:`fort-saint-jean`,name:`Fort Saint-Jean`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`fort`,`history`,`gardens`,`viewpoint`,`free`],area:`Vieux-Port`,lat:43.2955,lng:5.3629,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The medieval and 17th-century fortress guarding the harbour entrance, now threaded with ramparts walks and Mediterranean gardens that link the Panier to the MuCEM.`,tip:`Enter from the Panier side via the upper footbridge by the Église Saint-Laurent for the best approach.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fort Saint-Jean (Marseille)`},{id:`marseille-cathedral`,name:`Marseille Cathedral`,localName:`Cathédrale La Major`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`architecture`,`byzantine`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Joliette (J4)`,lat:43.29966,lng:5.36443,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A colossal 19th-century cathedral in striped green and white stone, its domes and marble-and-mosaic interior towering over the modern docks.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; pair it with the arcades of the Voûtes de la Major below for a coffee by the water.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Marseille Cathedral`},{id:`le-panier`,name:`Le Panier`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`old-town`,`street-art`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Le Panier`,lat:43.29857,lng:5.36873,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Marseille's oldest quarter, a hill of steep stairways, washing lines, pastel façades and street art, with small squares, soap shops and ateliers tucked into its lanes.`,tip:`Start at the Montée des Accoules stairs from the Vieux-Port and wander up to Place de Lenche for its view of Notre-Dame de la Garde.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Le Panier`},{id:`vieille-charite`,name:`La Vieille Charité`,category:`museum`,tags:[`architecture`,`baroque`,`archaeology`,`rainy-day`],area:`Le Panier`,lat:43.29978,lng:5.368,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`A former 17th-century almshouse whose three tiers of arcades surround a domed baroque chapel, now home to museums of Mediterranean archaeology and African, Oceanic and American art.`,tip:`The courtyard and chapel are free to wander; the museums inside are closed on Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Vieille Charité`},{id:`chateau-d-if`,name:`Château d'If`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`island`,`fortress`,`boat`,`history`,`literature`],area:`Frioul Islands`,lat:43.2799,lng:5.32505,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`The island fortress-prison made famous by The Count of Monte Cristo, reached by a 20-minute ferry from the Vieux-Port, with dungeon cells and sweeping views back to the city.`,tip:`Boats are cancelled when the mistral blows hard; buy a combined If and Frioul ferry ticket to hop on to the larger islands afterwards.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Château d'If`},{id:`frioul-islands`,name:`Frioul Islands`,localName:`Archipel du Frioul`,category:`nature`,tags:[`island`,`swimming`,`hiking`,`boat`,`coves`],area:`Frioul Islands`,lat:43.27997,lng:5.3066,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`A car-free archipelago of bare white limestone a half-hour ferry ride out, with trails between quiet coves of clear water and the ruins of an old quarantine hospital.`,tip:`There is almost no shade: bring water, a hat and swimming gear, and check the last ferry time back.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Frioul archipelago`},{id:`vallon-des-auffes`,name:`Vallon des Auffes`,category:`culture`,tags:[`fishing-port`,`photo-spot`,`seafood`,`free`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Corniche`,lat:43.28549,lng:5.35057,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A tiny fishermen's cove hidden beneath a stone viaduct of the Corniche, crowded with brightly painted pointu boats, cabanons and a couple of famous seafood restaurants.`,tip:`Take the stairs down from the Corniche; come at sunset and stay for bouillabaisse at Chez Fonfon.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Vallon des Auffes`},{id:`corniche-kennedy`,name:`Corniche Kennedy`,localName:`Corniche Président-John-Fitzgerald-Kennedy`,category:`nature`,tags:[`seafront`,`walking`,`sunset`,`viewpoint`,`free`],area:`Corniche`,lat:43.2805,lng:5.3519,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A five-kilometre seafront road and promenade along cliffs and coves, with the longest bench in the world, views of the Frioul islands and locals leaping off the rocks into the sea.`,tip:`Walk or cycle from the Plage des Catalans towards the Prado beaches as the sun drops behind the islands.`,indoor:!1},{id:`plage-des-catalans`,name:`Catalans Beach`,localName:`Plage des Catalans`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`swimming`,`volleyball`,`free`],area:`Corniche`,lat:43.2901,lng:5.355,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The sandy city beach closest to the centre, a short walk from the Vieux-Port, busy with beach-volleyball players and swimmers on summer afternoons.`,tip:`Arrive early on summer weekends; the water is calmer and clearer in the morning.`,indoor:!1},{id:`plages-du-prado`,name:`Prado Beaches`,localName:`Plages du Prado`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`swimming`,`park`,`kids`,`free`],area:`Prado`,lat:43.2606,lng:5.3745,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A long string of lawns and pebble-and-sand beaches built on landfill south of the centre, watched over by a replica of Michelangelo's David, with lifeguards and windsurfing in summer.`,tip:`The Escale Borély end has cafés and restaurants for a sunset drink after a swim.`,indoor:!1},{id:`parc-borely`,name:`Borély Park`,localName:`Parc Borély`,category:`family`,tags:[`park`,`gardens`,`lake`,`kids`,`free`],area:`Prado`,lat:43.2593,lng:5.3817,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A grand park behind the Prado beaches with a French formal garden, a boating lake, a botanical garden and pedal-cars for children, framed by an 18th-century château.`,tip:`Rent a rosalie (pedal cart) for the kids, then cross to the beach for an ice cream.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parc Borély`},{id:`chateau-borely`,name:`Château Borély`,localName:`Musée des Arts décoratifs, de la Faïence et de la Mode`,category:`museum`,tags:[`decorative-arts`,`fashion`,`ceramics`,`rainy-day`],area:`Prado`,lat:43.25866,lng:5.38194,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:3,description:`An 18th-century merchant's château in Parc Borély housing Marseille's museum of decorative arts, faience and fashion, with period salons and haute-couture pieces.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; combine it with a stroll in the park and a swim at the Prado beaches.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Château Borély`},{id:`palais-longchamp`,name:`Palais Longchamp`,category:`museum`,tags:[`architecture`,`fountain`,`art`,`natural-history`,`rainy-day`],area:`Longchamp`,lat:43.3047,lng:5.3947,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`A theatrical 19th-century colonnade and cascading fountain built to celebrate the canal that brought water to the city, with the fine-arts museum in one wing and the natural history museum in the other.`,tip:`The museums close on Mondays; the gardens behind the palace are free and good for a picnic.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palais Longchamp`},{id:`marseille-history-museum`,name:`Marseille History Museum`,localName:`Musée d'Histoire de Marseille`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`archaeology`,`greek`,`roman`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vieux-Port`,lat:43.29806,lng:5.37583,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`One of the largest city-history museums in France, telling 26 centuries of Marseille from Greek Massalia onward, beside the excavated ancient harbour in the Jardin des Vestiges.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; do not miss the remarkably preserved Roman-era merchant ship on display.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Marseille History Museum`},{id:`musee-cantini`,name:`Musée Cantini`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`modern-art`,`surrealism`,`rainy-day`],area:`Préfecture`,lat:43.2907,lng:5.3779,durationHours:1.25,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:3,description:`A 17th-century mansion holding the city's modern art collection, strong on Fauvism and Surrealism, rehung in 2026 with a new route through 20th-century and contemporary works.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; it is a short walk from the shopping streets around Rue Paradis.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée Cantini`},{id:`abbey-of-saint-victor`,name:`Abbey of Saint-Victor`,localName:`Abbaye Saint-Victor`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`crypt`,`medieval`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`Saint-Victor`,lat:43.2906,lng:5.366,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:2,rating:4,description:`A fortress-like abbey church above the south side of the port, whose atmospheric crypts hold early Christian sarcophagi and chapels dating back to the 5th century.`,tip:`The church is free and the crypt costs a couple of euros; buy navettes at the Four des Navettes bakery just below.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Abbey of St Victor, Marseille`},{id:`four-des-navettes`,name:`Four des Navettes`,category:`food`,tags:[`bakery`,`historic`,`souvenir`,`local-specialty`],area:`Saint-Victor`,lat:43.29085,lng:5.36555,durationHours:.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`Marseille's oldest bakery, in business since 1781, still baking boat-shaped, orange-blossom navette biscuits in its original wood-fired oven.`,tip:`A bag of navettes keeps for weeks and makes a classic Marseille souvenir.`,indoor:!0},{id:`jardin-du-pharo`,name:`Pharo Gardens`,localName:`Jardin du Pharo`,category:`nature`,tags:[`gardens`,`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`night-view`,`free`],area:`Pharo`,lat:43.2928,lng:5.3607,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The lawns around Napoleon III's seaside palace at the harbour mouth, with one of the best views over the Vieux-Port, Fort Saint-Jean and the MuCEM.`,tip:`Bring a drink and watch the sunset over the Frioul islands, then see the port lights come on below.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Palais du Pharo`},{id:`cosquer-mediterranee`,name:`Cosquer Méditerranée`,category:`family`,tags:[`prehistory`,`cave-art`,`replica`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Joliette (J4)`,lat:43.2964,lng:5.3629,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:23,rating:4,description:`A full-scale replica of the Cosquer Cave, an underwater Paleolithic cave in the Calanques, toured in small pods past painted penguins, horses and stencilled hands.`,tip:`Book a timed slot online, especially on weekends and in school holidays.`,indoor:!0},{id:`les-terrasses-du-port`,name:`Les Terrasses du Port`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`mall`,`sea-view`,`terrace`,`rainy-day`],area:`Joliette (J4)`,lat:43.308,lng:5.365,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A modern shopping centre on the ferry docks with a long public terrace overlooking the cruise ships and the open sea.`,tip:`Even if you are not shopping, the terrace is a pleasant free sunset viewpoint.`,indoor:!0},{id:`noailles-market`,name:`Noailles Market`,localName:`Marché des Capucins`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`spices`,`street-food`,`multicultural`],area:`Noailles`,lat:43.2962,lng:5.3801,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:4,description:`Marseille's 'belly', a loud, fragrant tangle of streets just off the Canebière with North African grocers, spice shops, fishmongers and the daily Capucins produce market.`,tip:`Go in the morning, keep an eye on your bag in the crowds, and try a Tunisian sandwich or a mint tea.`,indoor:!1},{id:`cours-julien`,name:`Cours Julien`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`street-art`,`live-music`,`bohemian`],area:`Cours Julien`,lat:43.2942,lng:5.383,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`The city's creative quarter, every wall covered in graffiti, where terrace bars, small concert venues and cheap world-food restaurants spill around a long pedestrian square after dark.`,tip:`Walk the street-art stairs of Rue Pastoret and Rue des Trois Rois before settling into a terrace for the evening.`,indoor:!1},{id:`opera-de-marseille`,name:`Marseille Opera`,localName:`Opéra de Marseille`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`art-deco`,`performance`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vieux-Port`,lat:43.294,lng:5.3768,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:3,description:`An Art Deco opera house behind the Vieux-Port staging opera, ballet and symphonic concerts in a red-and-gold auditorium rebuilt after a fire in 1919.`,tip:`Book ahead for opera nights; last-minute and under-28 tickets are much cheaper.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Opéra de Marseille`},{id:`stade-velodrome`,name:`Orange Vélodrome`,localName:`Stade Vélodrome`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`football`,`stadium`,`atmosphere`,`om`],area:`Rond-Point du Prado`,lat:43.26981,lng:5.39586,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`The home of Olympique de Marseille, where a night match brings 65,000 fans, huge tifos and one of the most passionate crowds in European football.`,tip:`Only on match nights (season runs August–May), so check the OM fixture list first; buy tickets only from the official OM site.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Stade Vélodrome`},{id:`friche-la-belle-de-mai`,name:`La Friche la Belle de Mai`,category:`culture`,tags:[`arts-centre`,`rooftop`,`industrial`,`sunset`,`free`],area:`Belle de Mai`,lat:43.3105,lng:5.3905,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A former tobacco factory turned sprawling arts centre with exhibitions, a skate park, a bookshop and a huge rooftop terrace for sunset drinks and summer DJ sets.`,tip:`The rooftop is busiest on summer evenings; check the programme for exhibitions and concerts.`,indoor:!1},{id:`cite-radieuse`,name:`Cité Radieuse`,localName:`Unité d'habitation Le Corbusier`,category:`culture`,tags:[`architecture`,`le-corbusier`,`unesco`,`modernism`,`free`],area:`Sainte-Anne`,lat:43.26144,lng:5.3964,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Le Corbusier's 1952 concrete 'vertical village', a UNESCO-listed apartment block with an inner shopping street, a hotel and a rooftop once used as a school playground.`,tip:`Residents live here, so stick to the public shopping floor; the tourist office runs guided tours that visit an apartment.`,indoor:!0},{id:`calanques-boat-cruise`,name:`Calanques Boat Cruise`,category:`nature`,tags:[`boat`,`calanques`,`cliffs`,`sightseeing`],area:`Vieux-Port`,lat:43.295,lng:5.3745,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:38,rating:4,description:`A cruise from the Vieux-Port along the white cliffs of the Calanques National Park, nosing into turquoise inlets such as Sormiou, Morgiou and En-Vau that are otherwise reached only on foot.`,tip:`Sailings are cancelled in strong mistral; sit on the right (starboard) side on the way out for the best cliff views.`,indoor:!1},{id:`les-goudes`,name:`Les Goudes`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`fishing-village`,`swimming`,`seafood`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Les Goudes`,lat:43.217,lng:5.348,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:2,rating:4,description:`A rocky fishing hamlet at the end of the coast road, where the city stops and the Calanques begin, with swimming off the rocks and simple seafood terraces.`,tip:`Bus 19 then 20 gets you there; walk on to Callelongue for the start of the coastal trails.`,indoor:!1},{id:`calanque-de-sugiton`,name:`Calanque de Sugiton Hike`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`hiking`,`calanques`,`swimming`,`viewpoint`],area:`Calanques (Luminy)`,lat:43.2122,lng:5.4533,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:2,rating:5,description:`A rocky hike from the Luminy campus over the Col de Sugiton down to a turquoise inlet beneath sheer limestone walls, one of the most beautiful swims on the coast.`,tip:`In summer free online booking is required for Sugiton, and the massifs close on high fire-risk days: check the park website the evening before.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Calanque de Sugiton`},{id:`cassis`,name:`Cassis`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`harbour`,`calanques`,`wine`,`swimming`],area:`Cassis (25 km)`,lat:43.2139,lng:5.5382,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`A pastel fishing port beneath Europe's highest sea cliff, Cap Canaille, with boat trips to the Calanques of Port-Miou, Port-Pin and En-Vau and crisp local white wine.`,tip:`The station is 3 km above town, so take the shuttle bus down; boats to the Calanques leave from the harbour.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Cassis`},{id:`aix-en-provence`,name:`Aix-en-Provence`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`old-town`,`cezanne`,`markets`,`fountains`],area:`Aix-en-Provence (30 km)`,lat:43.5269,lng:5.4473,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Cézanne's elegant hometown, half an hour away by bus, with the plane-tree-shaded Cours Mirabeau, mossy fountains, ochre mansions and lively morning markets.`,tip:`Go on a Tuesday, Thursday or Saturday morning for the biggest markets, and try calissons, the local almond sweets.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Aix-en-Provence`}],foods:[{name:`Bouillabaisse`,description:`The great Marseille fish stew: rockfish and other local fish simmered with saffron, fennel and tomato, served as a broth with croutons and rouille, then the fish.`},{name:`Chickpea fritters`,localName:`Panisses`,description:`Thick chickpea-flour batter set, sliced into fingers and deep-fried until crisp outside and creamy within.`},{name:`Navette biscuits`,localName:`Navettes`,description:`Hard, boat-shaped biscuits scented with orange-blossom water, traditionally eaten at Candlemas but sold all year.`},{name:`Lamb tripe parcels`,localName:`Pieds paquets`,description:`Little parcels of lamb tripe stuffed with salt pork, garlic and parsley, slow-cooked with lamb trotters in white wine and tomato.`},{name:`Grand aïoli`,localName:`Aïoli garni`,description:`Poached salt cod, boiled vegetables, eggs and sometimes snails, served with a big bowl of pungent garlic mayonnaise.`},{name:`Chichi doughnuts`,localName:`Chichis frégis`,description:`L'Estaque's long, ridged doughnuts made with chickpea and wheat flour, fried and rolled in sugar, eaten hot from a paper cone.`}]},{id:`bordeaux`,name:`Bordeaux`,lat:44.8378,lng:-.5792,timezone:`Europe/Paris`,tagline:`Golden stone quays, grand wine and a river that mirrors it all`,description:`The capital of the world's most famous wine region curves along the Garonne in a crescent of honey-coloured 18th-century façades, with a UNESCO-listed old town, a buzzing riverside, the striking Cité du Vin and legendary vineyards just beyond the city.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`place-de-la-bourse`,name:`Place de la Bourse`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`square`,`architecture`,`riverside`,`free`,`unesco`],area:`Saint-Pierre`,lat:44.84133,lng:-.56969,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Bordeaux's grandest square, a sweeping 18th-century royal ensemble open to the Garonne, centred on the Fountain of the Three Graces.`,tip:`Come back after dark, when the façades glow gold and reflect in the water mirror opposite.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Place de la Bourse, Bordeaux`},{id:`miroir-d-eau-bordeaux`,name:`Water Mirror`,localName:`Miroir d'eau`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`photo-spot`,`kids`,`free`,`night-view`,`riverside`],area:`Saint-Pierre`,lat:44.84185,lng:-.56965,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The world's largest reflecting pool, a thin sheet of water on granite that perfectly mirrors the Place de la Bourse and periodically vanishes into a cloud of mist.`,tip:`Wait for the mist cycle for the best photos; it is switched off in winter, roughly November to March.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Miroir d'eau`},{id:`bordeaux-cathedral`,name:`Bordeaux Cathedral`,localName:`Cathédrale Saint-André`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`gothic`,`architecture`,`unesco`,`free`],area:`Pey-Berland`,lat:44.83774,lng:-.57751,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A soaring Gothic cathedral where the future Eleanor of Aquitaine married Louis VII in 1137, with a sculpted Royal Portal and a vast, airy nave.`,tip:`Look for the sculpted Royal Door on the north side, one of the finest Gothic portals in southwest France.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Bordeaux Cathedral`},{id:`tour-pey-berland`,name:`Pey-Berland Tower`,localName:`Tour Pey-Berland`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`tower`,`viewpoint`,`gothic`,`climb`],area:`Pey-Berland`,lat:44.83738,lng:-.57682,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:4,description:`The cathedral's free-standing 15th-century bell tower, topped by a gilded Virgin, with 231 steps up to the best rooftop panorama of the old town.`,tip:`Go at opening to climb before the narrow spiral stair gets busy; not suited to anyone uneasy in tight spaces.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Tour Pey-Berland`},{id:`grand-theatre-de-bordeaux`,name:`Grand Théâtre de Bordeaux`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`architecture`,`performance`,`iconic`],area:`Triangle d'Or`,lat:44.84273,lng:-.57427,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A neoclassical temple of the arts from 1780, fronted by twelve columns and statues of muses, with a gilded blue-and-gold auditorium hosting the city's opera and ballet.`,tip:`Last-minute and under-28 tickets are often much cheaper; daytime guided visits are possible on some days.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grand Théâtre de Bordeaux`},{id:`grosse-cloche`,name:`Grosse Cloche`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`gate`,`medieval`,`bell`,`photo-spot`,`free`],area:`Saint-Éloi`,lat:44.83591,lng:-.57156,durationHours:.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A medieval belfry gate with twin pointed towers and a giant bell, once the bell tower of the old town hall and still on the city's coat of arms.`,indoor:!1},{id:`porte-cailhau`,name:`Porte Cailhau`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`gate`,`medieval`,`viewpoint`,`riverside`],area:`Saint-Pierre`,lat:44.8396,lng:-.56946,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A fairy-tale 15th-century city gate on the quays, built to celebrate a French royal victory, with a small exhibition and river views from the top.`,tip:`Even if you skip the climb, walk through the arch into the lanes of the Saint-Pierre quarter.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Porte Cailhau`},{id:`basilique-saint-michel-bordeaux`,name:`Basilica of Saint-Michel`,localName:`Basilique Saint-Michel`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`gothic`,`neighbourhood`,`market`,`free`],area:`Saint-Michel`,lat:44.83449,lng:-.56684,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A flamboyant Gothic basilica with a separate needle-like spire, the tallest in southern France, rising over a multicultural square of cafés and weekend flea markets.`,tip:`Come on a Sunday morning for the market around the square, then lunch in the neighbourhood.`,indoor:!0},{id:`rue-sainte-catherine-bordeaux`,name:`Rue Sainte-Catherine`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`pedestrian`,`shops`,`high-street`,`free`],area:`Centre`,lat:44.839,lng:-.5736,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A pedestrian shopping street over a kilometre long, among the longest in Europe, running from the Grand Théâtre to the Place de la Victoire.`,tip:`Duck into the side streets around Rue Saint-Rémi and Place du Parlement for independent boutiques.`,indoor:!1},{id:`musee-d-aquitaine`,name:`Musée d'Aquitaine`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`archaeology`,`rainy-day`],area:`Pey-Berland`,lat:44.83586,lng:-.57327,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`The region's history museum, from prehistoric Venus carvings and Roman Burdigala to the wine trade and Bordeaux's role in the Atlantic slave trade.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; permanent collections are free on the first Sunday of the month.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée d'Aquitaine`},{id:`musee-des-beaux-arts-de-bordeaux`,name:`Museum of Fine Arts of Bordeaux`,localName:`Musée des Beaux-Arts de Bordeaux`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`paintings`,`rainy-day`],area:`Pey-Berland`,lat:44.83785,lng:-.58107,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`Paintings from the Renaissance to the 20th century, with Delacroix, Rubens and Marquet, set in two wings flanking the gardens of the town hall.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays; check whether one wing is closed for works before going.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Musée des Beaux-Arts de Bordeaux`},{id:`madd-bordeaux`,name:`Museum of Decorative Arts and Design`,localName:`Musée des Arts décoratifs et du Design (madd)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`design`,`mansion`,`decorative-arts`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Pey-Berland`,lat:44.83837,lng:-.5798,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`An 18th-century town mansion furnished as an aristocrat's home, paired with lively design exhibitions in the former prison next door.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays; the courtyard café is a quiet spot for lunch.`,indoor:!0},{id:`capc-bordeaux`,name:`CAPC Contemporary Art Museum`,localName:`CAPC musée d'art contemporain`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`contemporary`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Chartrons`,lat:44.84874,lng:-.57043,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`Contemporary art shown in the cathedral-like arcaded nave of the Entrepôt Lainé, a 19th-century warehouse for colonial goods.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; the rooftop terrace and café are worth a look even between exhibitions.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`CAPC musée d'art contemporain de Bordeaux`},{id:`la-cite-du-vin`,name:`La Cité du Vin`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`wine`,`architecture`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`],area:`Bassins à Flot`,lat:44.86259,lng:-.55017,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:5,description:`A swirling, decanter-shaped wine museum on the Garonne with immersive, multisensory exhibits on wine cultures worldwide, ending with a tasting on the 8th-floor belvedere.`,tip:`Book a timed slot online and save the glass included with your ticket for the panoramic top floor.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Cité du Vin`},{id:`bassins-des-lumieres`,name:`Bassins des Lumières`,category:`culture`,tags:[`digital-art`,`immersive`,`submarine-base`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Bassins à Flot`,lat:44.87175,lng:-.56018,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`Giant immersive projections of great painters flooding the walls and water of a colossal Second World War submarine base, one of the largest digital art centres in the world.`,tip:`Book online; the shows loop, so you can stay for a second viewing from a different spot.`,indoor:!0},{id:`cap-sciences`,name:`Cap Sciences`,category:`family`,tags:[`science`,`interactive`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Bassins à Flot`,lat:44.8594,lng:-.5535,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A hands-on science centre in a former riverside hangar, with rotating interactive exhibitions aimed at children and curious adults.`,tip:`Check the website for current exhibitions and opening days, which vary out of school holidays.`,indoor:!0},{id:`esplanade-des-quinconces`,name:`Esplanade des Quinconces`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`square`,`monument`,`fountain`,`free`],area:`Quinconces`,lat:44.84461,lng:-.57303,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`One of the largest city squares in Europe, anchored by the towering Girondins monument with its dramatic bronze fountains of horses and allegories.`,tip:`Funfairs and fairs take over the square in spring and autumn.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Place des Quinconces`},{id:`jardin-public-bordeaux`,name:`Jardin Public`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`garden`,`picnic`,`kids`,`free`],area:`Chartrons`,lat:44.84889,lng:-.57659,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An elegant English-style park laid out in the 18th century, with a pond, a botanical garden, old trees and a puppet theatre for children.`,tip:`The Guignol Guérin puppet show is a classic for kids on Wednesday and weekend afternoons.`,indoor:!1},{id:`chartrons`,name:`Chartrons`,category:`culture`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`antiques`,`wine-merchants`,`walking`,`free`],area:`Chartrons`,lat:44.8538,lng:-.5718,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The old wine merchants' quarter, now a village-like district of antique shops, concept stores and café terraces along Rue Notre-Dame.`,tip:`Sunday morning brings the Marché des Quais to the riverside nearby, with oysters and white wine.`,indoor:!1},{id:`marche-des-capucins`,name:`Marché des Capucins`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`oysters`,`local`,`rainy-day`],area:`Capucins`,lat:44.8308,lng:-.5681,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`Bordeaux's 'belly', a covered market where locals gather at the oyster counters, cheese stalls and tapas bars from early morning.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; weekends are liveliest, best before noon for an oysters-and-white-wine brunch.`,indoor:!0},{id:`halles-de-bacalan`,name:`Halles de Bacalan`,category:`food`,tags:[`food-hall`,`local-produce`,`lunch`,`rainy-day`],area:`Bassins à Flot`,lat:44.8623,lng:-.5499,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A modern food hall opposite the Cité du Vin, where around twenty southwest producers serve oysters, charcuterie, cheese and wine at shared tables.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; pair it with a visit to the Cité du Vin across the road.`,indoor:!0},{id:`darwin-ecosysteme`,name:`Darwin Écosystème`,category:`culture`,tags:[`street-art`,`skatepark`,`alternative`,`market`,`hidden-gem`,`free`],area:`La Bastide`,lat:44.84925,lng:-.5595,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A former military barracks on the right bank turned into an alternative hub of graffiti, an indoor skatepark, organic grocers, a brewery and a huge canteen.`,tip:`Saturday brings an organic market; the canteen terrace is good for a lazy lunch.`,indoor:!1},{id:`jardin-botanique-de-la-bastide`,name:`Bastide Botanical Garden`,localName:`Jardin botanique de la Bastide`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`botanical`,`free`,`quiet`],area:`La Bastide`,lat:44.84401,lng:-.55517,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A contemporary botanical garden on the right bank, with a long display of regional landscapes, aquatic gardens and greenhouses, all free.`,tip:`Cross the Pont de Pierre on foot and combine with the right-bank riverside park for great views of the façades.`,indoor:!1},{id:`pont-jacques-chaban-delmas`,name:`Pont Jacques Chaban-Delmas`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`bridge`,`architecture`,`night-view`,`free`],area:`Bassins à Flot`,lat:44.85861,lng:-.55333,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Europe's longest vertical-lift bridge, its four tall pylons lit in blue at night, with a central deck that rises so tall ships can sail into the city.`,tip:`Walk across at dusk; if a big ship is due, you may see the deck lifted.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pont Jacques Chaban-Delmas`},{id:`pont-de-pierre-bordeaux`,name:`Stone Bridge`,localName:`Pont de pierre`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`bridge`,`historic`,`night-view`,`sunset`,`free`],area:`Saint-Michel`,lat:44.8381,lng:-.5626,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Napoleon's 17-arch brick-and-stone bridge, its arches matching the letters of his name, now car-free with the finest view of the golden quays at sunset.`,tip:`Walk it at sunset, then continue to the right bank for a full view of the lit-up Place de la Bourse.`,indoor:!1},{id:`quais-de-bordeaux`,name:`Bordeaux Riverside Quays`,localName:`Les Quais`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`riverside`,`cycling`,`walking`,`sunset`,`free`],area:`Quinconces`,lat:44.847,lng:-.5672,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Kilometres of car-free promenade along the left bank, with lawns, playgrounds, skaters and cyclists, linking the old town to the Chartrons and the Cité du Vin.`,tip:`Rent a city bike (Le Vélo) and ride from the Pont de Pierre to the Cité du Vin.`,indoor:!1},{id:`bordeaux-river-cruise`,name:`Garonne River Cruise`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`boat`,`river`,`sightseeing`,`sunset`],area:`Quinconces`,lat:44.8434,lng:-.5688,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A sightseeing cruise on the wide, tidal Garonne, gliding past the Port of the Moon façades and under the city bridges, with commentary or a glass of wine.`,tip:`Sunset sailings with a wine tasting are the most atmospheric; boats leave from the Quinconces pontoon.`,indoor:!1},{id:`bar-a-vin-civb`,name:`Bar à Vin of the Bordeaux Wine Council`,localName:`Bar à Vin du CIVB`,category:`food`,tags:[`wine`,`tasting`,`historic`,`rainy-day`],area:`Triangle d'Or`,lat:44.84298,lng:-.57376,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`The wine council's own bar in a grand 18th-century house, pouring dozens of Bordeaux wines by the glass at gentle prices, with expert sommeliers on hand.`,tip:`Closed Sundays; ask the sommeliers for a comparison flight of left- and right-bank reds.`,indoor:!0},{id:`saint-pierre-bars`,name:`Place du Parlement and Saint-Pierre bars`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`terraces`,`squares`,`late-night`],area:`Saint-Pierre`,lat:44.84035,lng:-.57121,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`The old town's cobbled squares, Place du Parlement and Place Saint-Pierre, fill up after dark with café terraces, wine bars and a cheerful crowd.`,tip:`Start with an apéritif on Place du Parlement, then drift through the lanes toward Place Saint-Pierre.`,indoor:!1},{id:`palais-gallien`,name:`Palais Gallien`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`roman`,`ruins`,`history`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Fondaudège`,lat:44.84578,lng:-.58156,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:4,rating:3,description:`The surprising remains of a 2nd-century Roman amphitheatre, its brick arches rising between houses in a quiet residential street.`,tip:`You can see much of it from the street; inside visits run mainly from spring to autumn.`,indoor:!1},{id:`parc-bordelais`,name:`Parc Bordelais`,category:`family`,tags:[`park`,`kids`,`playground`,`free`],area:`Caudéran`,lat:44.85238,lng:-.603,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A big 19th-century landscaped park loved by local families, with a lake, small farm animals, playgrounds and a little train for children.`,tip:`The mini train and pony rides run mostly on Wednesdays, weekends and school holidays.`,indoor:!1},{id:`saint-emilion`,name:`Saint-Émilion`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`medieval`,`unesco`,`village`],area:`Libournais (40 km)`,lat:44.89421,lng:-.15514,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`A honey-stone medieval village on a hillside of vines, with a vast underground monolithic church, steep lanes and celebrated wine châteaux all around.`,tip:`Trains from Bordeaux take about 35 minutes; book an underground church tour at the tourist office and try the local macarons.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Saint-Émilion`},{id:`dune-du-pilat`,name:`Dune of Pilat`,localName:`Dune du Pilat`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`dune`,`beach`,`viewpoint`,`sunset`],area:`Bassin d'Arcachon (65 km)`,lat:44.58944,lng:-1.21361,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:5,description:`Europe's tallest sand dune, over 100 m high, with views of the Atlantic, the Arcachon Bay and a sea of pine forest, combined with oysters in Arcachon.`,tip:`Take the train to Arcachon (about 50 minutes) then the bus; parking is paid, and the summit is windy, so bring a layer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Dune of Pilat`},{id:`medoc-chateaux-pauillac`,name:`Médoc Wine Châteaux (Pauillac)`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`chateaux`,`tasting`,`countryside`],area:`Médoc (55 km)`,lat:45.19889,lng:-.74889,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:110,rating:4,description:`The Route des Châteaux through the Médoc, home of First Growths such as Lafite, Latour and Mouton Rothschild, with grand estates rising above the vines.`,tip:`Most châteaux need booking ahead; a guided tour from Bordeaux solves the driving after tastings.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pauillac`}],foods:[{name:`Canelé`,localName:`Canelé`,description:`A small fluted cake with a dark, caramelised crust and a soft, custardy centre scented with rum and vanilla.`},{name:`Bordeaux-style rib steak`,localName:`Entrecôte à la bordelaise`,description:`A rib steak grilled, traditionally over vine cuttings, and served with a red-wine, shallot and bone-marrow sauce.`},{name:`Arcachon oysters with sausages`,localName:`Huîtres et crépinettes`,description:`Briny oysters from the Arcachon Bay eaten with small hot pork crépinette sausages and a glass of white Entre-Deux-Mers.`},{name:`Lamprey Bordeaux-style`,localName:`Lamproie à la bordelaise`,description:`River lamprey slowly stewed with leeks in a dark sauce of red wine and its own blood, a rich spring speciality.`},{name:`Porcini Bordeaux-style`,localName:`Cèpes à la bordelaise`,description:`Sliced porcini mushrooms pan-fried in oil with shallots, garlic and parsley, a classic autumn dish.`},{name:`Duck breast`,localName:`Magret de canard`,description:`A thick fattened-duck breast seared with crisp skin and served pink, often with potatoes cooked in duck fat.`}]}]};export{e as france};